'' SIZEOF and LEN over an ARRAY measure its ELEMENT -- fbc's rule, measured on
'' fbc-modern 1.20.0 (2026-09-19) by compiling and running every line of the source.
''
'' The golden holds the whole fold sequence, e1..e11 then s1..s5 in source order. The
'' assertions below are the ones worth naming.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/sizeof-array.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0

'' THE STORAGE IS UNCHANGED, which is the whole point of the distinction: 'm' is still
'' the 24 bytes of a 2 x 3 array of long, and sizeof( m ) is 4.
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg m size 24
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg sa size 72
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg t_ size 24

'' THE ARRAY OF UDTs USED TO LOWER NOTHING AT ALL -- the fallback looked an ARRAY type
'' up in the UDT table, found nothing and declined, taking the statement with it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok

'' AND THE CONSTANT EVALUATOR'S HALF: 'dim c2( sizeof( b0 ) to 4 )' runs 1 to 4, not
'' 4 to 4. The bounds are the last two arguments.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_ArrayRedimEx(@c2, 4, -1, 0, 1, %25, %26)
'' GOLDEN: expected/sizeof-array.out
